# Ansible workshop working agreements

- Inspect README.adoc and the relevant workshop module before editing.
- Keep changes within the requested module and explain the resulting behavior.
- Target RHEL managed nodes; account for macOS differences on the control host.
- Use fully qualified Ansible module names and prefer idempotent modules to shell.
- Use example inventory values; keep credentials out of playbooks and Git.
- Use the user's existing working Ansible installation. If it needs environment
  activation, use the user-provided command or absolute executable path. If that
  information is missing and Ansible is unavailable, ask for the environment details.
- Validate changed playbooks with ansible-playbook --syntax-check when available.
- Run commands against managed hosts only when the user has authorized the target
  inventory and task. Check mode can still contact hosts and is not full isolation.
- Report checks performed and any checks that could not run.
